      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Page%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1957 as housing for Glen Canyon Dam workers, Page incorporated as a town in 1975.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Page%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Perched atop Manson Mesa, Page sits 4,300 feet above sea level and 600 feet above Lake Powell.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Page%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Page hosts two of the western U.S.'s largest power plants: the 1.29‑million‑kW Glen Canyon Dam and the 2.25‑million‑kW Navajo Generating Station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
